    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87870" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προ-κρούω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beat out</i> and so <i>stretch,</i> whence the name of
			the robber <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προκρούστης,</span> who
			stretched all his captives on the same bed, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐλαττόνων τοὺς πόδας προέκρουεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					4.59
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>attack,</i>
			
				Dor.
			
			impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὤκροον </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόκροον</span> codd.) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1252
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> sens. obsc.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1017
			</span></i>.</div>
